            "review_title": "Review at BackYard Beer Garden",
            "review_text": "Mao D\nHanoi, Vietnam1 contribution\n0\nDinning in a traditional Vietnamese Vegetable Garden in the centre of Hanoi\nJul 2015 • Friends\nThis was a wonderful experience. Imagine sitting in a traditional Vietnamese garden surrounded with vegetable patches, ponds, eclectic outdoor furniture and fruit trees. The menu is Vietnamese tapas, with many vegetarian options available. The smell from the bbq was incredible so we made sure we tried the speciality chicken drum sticks and the pork spare ribs. Both were so flavoursome and delicious. They serve fresh craft beers, international wines, fresh fruit juices and what I loved was that most of the vegetables the chefs use for cooking come direct from the garden you are sitting around.\n\nThe total ambience of Backyard beer garden is wonderful. On a hot summers night in Hanoi its the best place to be as the garden is close to the West Lake so there was a lovely breeze.\n\nIf you are living or travelling in Hanoi make sure you check out Backyard beer garden it is a total hidden gem but well worth the effort to find it. These are the type of places you dream about finding when you travel and the places you can't stop dreaming about after you leave. I am still dreaming of it\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten August 14, 2015",
